@startuml phased_run
title Phases, not a loop: swaps per run, not per question

skinparam wrapWidth 240

start

partition "Phase 1, retrieve (8 GB card)" {
  :one embeddings batch for the whole set (bge-m3);
  :hybrid search per question,
  a wide pool when reranking;
}

:the card checked here, before the generator is paid for;
note right
  The embedder is unloaded, and the generator with it.
end note

partition "Phase 2, rerank" {
  :flatten to pairs:
  100 questions x 20 candidates = 2000;
  :one scoring call for all of them,
  vllm-rerank takes the card;
  :slice the scores back per question, keep top k;
}

:the card handed back, vllm-rerank put to sleep;

partition "Phase 3, generate" {
  :answer from the context that is already prepared
  (llama3.1:8b);
  :question_log and the config snapshot:
  rerank, device, k, phased;
}

:on EVERY exit, not only the last line:
embedder and generator unloaded; <<#fff3cd>>
note right
  So a refusal does not leave its own
  generator on the card for the retry.
end note
stop
@enduml
